{"content":[{"c":["NAIN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Village in southern Galilee near the border of Samaria. It is the location of the miracle in which Jesus brought a dead man back to life (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.7.11","r":"Luke.7.11","rawR":"Luke.7.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.7.11","value":"Luke.7.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 7:11"},"). The man was the son of a widow who lived in this village."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Nain","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Lk 7:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.7.11","rawQueryValue":"Luke.7.11","sourceRefExact":"Luke.7.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"dd9e49b98d0d1f0743d0c824ce08ca4e46ce80836530b56ed01ca3c094c82ebb","sourceItemName":"Nain","sourceItemOrder":38,"sourceMember":"Articles/N.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Nain","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Nain","title":"Nain","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}